diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index 61db2da465..e3b90723c0 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -208,3 +208,7 @@ agents/
 # drift-details.txt) — test-run residue, never committed.
 /release-notes.md
 /drift-details.txt
+
+# gh-2096 leg: coverage2/ scratch run swept by a WIP auto-save — same
+# artifact class as coverage/ (gh-1033 lineage).
+coverage2/
diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 986a1eb9a3..79437d1ed5 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -13,6 +13,27 @@ block a release again.

 ## Unreleased

+- fix(gh-2096): auto-compact no longer re-pays the judge budget on every
+  run when the configured smol class cannot answer within it, and a judge
+  timeout no longer kills the retry. Three engine changes: (1) the
+  judge call runs under a PER-CALL child cancel token — a budget expiry
+  aborts only the in-flight call while the retry and the later LM stages
+  keep the run-wide token live (previously the first timeout cancelled
+  the shared token and the retry died born-cancelled in ~75 ms); (2) the
+  consecutive judge-failure counter is persisted per session as additive
+  `structured_judge_health` custom records (newest wins; no migrations —
+  old sessions load byte-identical), so the #541 deterministic fallback
+  latches ACROSS runs: while latched, auto-compact skips the judge
+  entirely (deterministic hide, receipt says "budget unwinnable for the
+  configured class") and pays ONE probe call per `judgeProbeAfter`
+  window (default 10 min; a changed model class probes at once) — the
+  probe unlatches on success, failure re-arms; (3) the named judge
+  timeout line (#541 AC3) now carries the attempt shape — input entries,
+  est. tokens, elapsed — so a slow-reasoning class is distinguishable
+  from a wedged endpoint in logs alone; the pass reports gain
+  `judgeInputEntries`/`judgeInputTokens`/`judgeElapsedMs`/`judgeLatched`.
+  Docs: the smol/judge model-class rule (a class that answers within the
+  budget, or a budget sized to the class) in `docs/agents/providers.md`.
 - fix(gh-2075): the daily-publish macOS legs no longer depend on the
   package:sqlite3 native-assets hook's single un-retried build-time
   download. The `build-macos.yml` app-build and CLI-bundle steps now
diff --git a/docs/agents/providers.md b/docs/agents/providers.md
index 41914b9882..a1c481117a 100644
--- a/docs/agents/providers.md
+++ b/docs/agents/providers.md
@@ -128,6 +128,21 @@ roles:
   smol: [openrouter/openai/gpt-4o-mini]   # keeps 300s
 ```

+Judge/smol model-class rule: the `smol` role also serves the structured
+compaction hide judge — ONE call under a fixed attempt budget
+(`compaction.judgeBudgetSeconds`, default 300 s) with a bounded input
+(newest 512 ledger entries). Pick a class that answers within that budget
+(a non-mandatory-reasoning class, or a budget sized to the class's
+thinking time); a mandatory-reasoning class behind a queueing gateway can
+make EVERY judge call hit the full budget. The engine defends itself: a
+judge that times out falls back to the deterministic judge-less hide
+after two consecutive failures, and the failure latches across runs —
+auto-compact then skips the judge (deterministic hide) and pays one
+probe call per window instead of the full budget per run. The named
+failure line carries the attempt shape (input entries, est. tokens,
+elapsed), so a slow-reasoning class reads differently from a wedged
+endpoint in logs.
+
 ## Vision helpers

 - `lib/src/model_roles/vision_models.dart` — shared vision heuristic (`modelIdSuggestsVision`, `visionMarker` picker checkmark, `inputModalitiesFor`): CLI model switches recompute `Model.input` from it and the model pickers show the ✓/✗ marker; `packages/fa_ui` re-exports it (one marker list for CLI and app).
diff --git a/lib/src/agent/auto_compactor.dart b/lib/src/agent/auto_compactor.dart
index 7f1b6cc178..783a537894 100644
--- a/lib/src/agent/auto_compactor.dart
+++ b/lib/src/agent/auto_compactor.dart
@@ -58,6 +58,10 @@ final class AutoCompactorPass {
     this.marginTokens,
     this.bandTokens,
     this.hideableRemaining,
+    this.judgeInputEntries,
+    this.judgeInputTokens,
+    this.judgeElapsedMs,
+    this.judgeLatched = false,
   });

   /// 1-based pass number.
@@ -107,6 +111,22 @@ final class AutoCompactorPass {
   /// gh-2044: remaining hideable-entry count at escalation time — a
   /// diagnostic count only. Null except on escalation passes.
   final int? hideableRemaining;
+
+  /// gh-2096 timeout diagnosis (judge-failure and probe receipts): the
+  /// judged attempt's input entry count. Null on every other pass.
+  final int? judgeInputEntries;
+
+  /// gh-2096: the judged attempt's input estimated-token size. Null on
+  /// every other pass.
+  final int? judgeInputTokens;
+
+  /// gh-2096: the wall-clock time the judged attempt consumed. Null on
+  /// every other pass.
+  final int? judgeElapsedMs;
+
+  /// gh-2096: whether this pass was decided by the cross-run judge-health
+  /// latch (a latched skip or a probe receipt).
+  final bool judgeLatched;
 }

 /// Hooks for a host UI to observe progress. Implementations should not
