## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | test/agent/auto_compactor_structured_budget_test.dart | 🚨 blocking stale 515 assertion — this pr introduces a deterministic test failure ci breakage the per call token change is the point of gh 2096 but the pre existing test whose body asserts the old mechanism this hunk s test — the stale assertion sits at line 351 14 lines below the changed line was not updated dart the engine killed the in flight call at the token not just the await the provider layer sees the abort 515 semantics kept expect budgetsource token iscancelled istrue line 351 on this branch the judge timeout cancels only the per call child token so budgetsource token stays live and the assertion fails reproduced twice on the pr branch dart test test agent auto compactor structured budget test dart plain name the hide judge budget kill → expected true actual false at 351 5 the full test compaction test agent sweep is 1050 passed 1 failed — this is the only failure verified passing on origin main in a clean worktree — the failure is introduced by this pr deterministic not flaky this pr s own new test asserts the opposite semantics structured judge health test dart expect budgetsource token iscancelled isfalse reason a judge timeout must not cancel the run wide budget token — the two tests now encode contradictory behavior and the old one loses fix update this test to gh 2096 semantics — assert the per call token was cancelled the provider layer still sees the abort 515 is preserved via the forwarded child token and the run wide budget token stayed live the engine code itself is correct only this stale assertion needs the update |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
